Question:A blood sample is taken from a 45 year old man after he has broken his overnight fast by eating three slices of toast and a boiled egg. Which one of the following will be at a higher concentration than if the blood sample had been taken before breakfast?
Options:
A) Alanine
B) Glucose
C) Ketone bodies
D) Non-esterified (free) fatty acids
Thought:
After an overnight fast, the body relies on glycogen stores and fat breakdown for energy. Consuming carbohydrates (toast) and protein (egg) post-fast will increase glucose levels. Glucose (B) rises immediately after eating, while ketone bodies and NEFA decrease due to glucose availability. Alanine levels are less affected. Thus, the correct answer is B.
Ground truth: B
Answer: B
